I'm too lazy to go match up the struct entries to
the template, but is one of those MR_POISON entries
a poison _attack_? If so, you'd really have a lot of
work to do, because I don't think attacks are sex
differentiated anywhere in NetHack, and in real
life, only the male platypus has the poison spurs.
You could perhaps follow the egg laying capacity for
a partial idea of where changes need to happen, I
guess, but they'd be more widespread than that.

Also, I object to any platypus being other than size
small; they are cryptozooids, and "large" just
doesn't work for that ecological niche.

Other than that, it's a heck of a good idea.

